The `GET` request to `/auth/admin/user-list/` endpoint returns a JSON response containing a list of user details. The response schema for the request is as follows:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "count": {
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "next": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "previous": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "first_name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "last_name": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "auth_type": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "uid": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "email": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "country": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "city": {
            "type": ["string", "null"]
          },
          "country_code": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "contact": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "photo": {
            "type": ["string", "null"]
          },
          "active": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "is_active": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "date_joined": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": ["first_name", "last_name", "auth_type", "uid", "email", "country", "country_code", "contact", "active", "is_active", "date_joined"]
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["count", "next", "previous", "results"]
}

 ```

### /auth/admin/reset-password/

This endpoint is used to reset the password for an admin user.

#### Request

The request should be sent as an HTTP POST to the specified URL. The request body should be of form-data type and include the following parameter:

- `email` (text): The email address of the admin user for whom the password needs to be reset.


#### Response

The response for this request will be in JSON format and may include the following key:

- `detail` (string): A message providing details about the password reset process.


#### JSON Schema

``` json
{
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "detail": {
            "type": "string"
        }
    }
}

 ```

The `GET` request to `/auth/admin/ip-logs/` endpoint retrieves a list of IP logs associated with admin authentication. The response is a JSON object with the following schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "count": {
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "next": {
      "type": ["string", "null"]
    },
    "previous": {
      "type": ["string", "null"]
    },
    "results": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "user": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "ip": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "region": {
            "type": ["string", "null"]
          },
          "blocked": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "created": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

 ```

### Auth Admin Custom Token

This endpoint allows the admin to generate a custom token.

#### Request Body

- form-data
    - email (text)
    - token (text)

#### Response

The response for this request can be represented as a JSON schema:

``` json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "data": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "idToken": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "refreshToken": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "expiresIn": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "isNewUser": {
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
}

 ```

